<sui>
    <head>
        <window state="normal"
                title="SimpleUI Script Test"
                width="900"
                height="640" />
        <link href="/assets/style.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    </head>
    <script href="/src/loading.cpp" /> <!-- loaded before the screen is drawn -->
    <body>
        <div class="sidebar">
            <button onclick="addone();"> Click to Add </button>
            <button onclick="toggleHighlight();"> Toggle highlight </button>
            <button onclick="recolorSidebar();"> Recolor </button>
        </div>

        <div class="content">
            <h1>SimpleUI scripts</h1>
            <p>This paragraph wraps across several lines so the inline formatter
               has to measure real glyph advances instead of guessing at
               character widths. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.</p>
            <p id="counter">0</p>
            <p id="badge">Buttons</p>
            <p>Click the buttons to run a handler and re-layout.<br />The counter
               above is a real DOM mutation.</p>
        </div>
    </body>
    <script href="/src/calculate.cpp" />
</sui>